WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.383 --> 00:00:03.935
- In Detroit over the last three years

00:00:03.935 --> 00:00:05.529
over 100,000 families have

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:07.612
had their water shut off.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:10.155
I can't touch water or drink water

00:00:10.155 --> 00:00:11.495
or be in contact with water

00:00:11.495 --> 00:00:13.103
without thinking about somebody

00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:14.270
not having it.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:22.481
My name is Monica Lewis-Patrick,

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:24.595
and I'm the President and CEO

00:00:24.595 --> 00:00:27.696
of We the People of Detroit.

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:31.692
We're committed to the
human right to water.

00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:33.132
Low income people in Detroit

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.958
are having a hard time paying

00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:36.416
their water bill.

00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.628
And they're getting their water shut off.

00:00:39.628 --> 00:00:40.736
When the water department comes out

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:41.846
to shut off the water,

00:00:41.846 --> 00:00:43.348
they mark it with a blue line

00:00:43.348 --> 00:00:44.738
and for many of the residents

00:00:44.738 --> 00:00:47.620
it's known as the blue line of shame.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.985
Some people's water is only off

00:00:48.985 --> 00:00:50.500
for a matter of days,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.568
others' water has been off

00:00:51.568 --> 00:00:54.280
as long as two to three years.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.948
The issue of not having access

00:00:55.948 --> 00:00:58.448
to water is a really big deal.

00:01:00.328 --> 00:01:02.068
You can lose custody of your children,

00:01:02.068 --> 00:01:03.505
you can lose your property,

00:01:03.505 --> 00:01:06.505
you can also lose your quality of health.

00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:10.322
It just doesn't sit well with me.

00:01:11.516 --> 00:01:14.804
Our job is really to meet that human need.

00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:16.394
Our services are for those families

00:01:16.394 --> 00:01:17.668
that can't afford to get their water

00:01:17.668 --> 00:01:18.918
turned back on.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.198
Our water primarily is donated

00:01:22.198 --> 00:01:24.556
and then we store it in
one of our water stations

00:01:24.556 --> 00:01:26.037
and then it is distributed

00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:29.476
out to the community based on need.

00:01:29.476 --> 00:01:30.985
The deliveries that we do every week

00:01:30.985 --> 00:01:32.836
makes sure that the client has enough

00:01:32.836 --> 00:01:35.308
water on an emergency basis

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:36.676
to do some basic things,

00:01:36.676 --> 00:01:38.081
flush the toilet, take care

00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:39.208
of their basic hygiene,

00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:40.791
prepare their food.

00:01:43.424 --> 00:01:45.328
Over the last year,

00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:49.064
we've served over a thousand families.

00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:50.561
Water can unite us.

00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:51.762
And so it's out of belovedness

00:01:51.762 --> 00:01:54.734
that we approach our water work.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.188
I always like to say
I didn't choose water,

00:01:56.188 --> 00:01:57.521
water chose me.

